// Title: Root Certificate Installed From Susp Locations
// ID: 5f6a601c-2ecb-498b-9c33-660362323afa
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-09
// Tags: attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1553.004
// Description: Adversaries may install a root certificate on a compromised system to avoid warnings when connecting to adversary controlled web servers.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "Import-Certificate") AND where(CommandLine ICONTAINS " -FilePath ") AND where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "Cert:\\LocalMachine\\Root")) AND (where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS ":\\Windows\\TEMP\\") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "\\Desktop\\") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "\\Downloads\\") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "\\Perflogs\\") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS ":\\Users\\Public\\")))
